WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.798
Cedar Vale renews its service and adds
a new recurring service

00:03.798 --> 00:04.992
in the same purchase.

00:05.242 --> 00:07.461
There is also a one-time commissioning
fee.

00:07.711 --> 00:11.830
The customer sees one purchase, but
Finance and Sales need to

00:11.830 --> 00:13.940
understand three different kinds of
value.

00:14.600 --> 00:18.776
In this fictional example, the old annual
recurring baseline is twelve

00:18.776 --> 00:19.699
thousand dollars.

00:19.949 --> 00:23.996
The new commitment covers one full
year, from January through December

00:23.996 --> 00:25.069
twenty twenty-seven.

00:25.319 --> 00:28.820
All amounts are in dollars, before tax,
with no discounts or

00:28.820 --> 00:29.543
proration.

00:30.200 --> 00:33.635
Calling the entire purchase new sales
overstates growth.

00:33.885 --> 00:36.295
Calling everything renewal hides
expansion.

00:36.545 --> 00:40.693
The answer starts by classifying the
components, then reconciling the

00:40.693 --> 00:44.439
customer total separately from the
change in recurring value.

00:45.100 --> 00:49.516
The twelve-thousand-dollar renewal
retains the existing recurring service.

00:49.766 --> 00:53.539
It contributes twelve thousand dollars
to the new recurring total, but

00:53.539 --> 00:55.142
zero incremental growth.

00:55.392 --> 00:59.232
We are carrying the baseline forward,
not creating that baseline again.

00:59.900 --> 01:03.079
The additional service adds three
thousand dollars per year.

01:03.329 --> 01:05.910
That is recurring expansion in this
example.

01:06.160 --> 01:09.479
Compare the products and
entitlements with the prior agreement

01:09.479 --> 01:13.179
so that an existing charge is not
accidentally labelled as a

01:13.179 --> 01:13.968
new service.

01:14.633 --> 01:17.806
The fifteen-hundred-dollar
commissioning fee belongs in the

01:17.806 --> 01:21.716
purchase reconciliation, but not in
annual recurring revenue.

01:21.966 --> 01:25.465
Its invoice and commission treatment
can follow separate rules.

01:25.715 --> 01:29.021
A payment being collected today does
not make it recurring.

01:29.700 --> 01:33.244
For recurring value, start with the
twelve-thousand-dollar opening

01:33.244 --> 01:33.881
baseline.

01:34.131 --> 01:36.585
There is no contraction or churn in this
case.

01:36.835 --> 01:39.011
Add three thousand dollars of
expansion.

01:39.261 --> 01:43.705
Closing annual recurring revenue is
fifteen thousand dollars, and recurring

01:43.705 --> 01:45.255
growth is three thousand.

01:45.933 --> 01:50.002
For the one-year purchase, add twelve
thousand renewal, three thousand

01:50.002 --> 01:52.483
expansion, and fifteen hundred
one-time work.

01:52.733 --> 01:55.442
That totals sixteen thousand five
hundred dollars.

01:55.692 --> 02:00.786
Keep this consideration total separate
from closing ARR, invoice cash, and

02:00.786 --> 02:01.943
recognized revenue.

02:02.600 --> 02:07.198
A common mistake is adding the old
twelve-thousand-dollar baseline to the

02:07.198 --> 02:10.301
entire new fifteen-thousand-dollar
recurring amount.

02:10.551 --> 02:12.898
That produces twenty-seven thousand
dollars.

02:13.148 --> 02:17.274
The renewal already carries the
retained baseline, so that calculation

02:17.274 --> 02:18.268
counts it twice.

02:18.933 --> 02:23.006
If one team manages the purchase, a
single commercial deal with

02:23.006 --> 02:26.485
classified components can keep the
customer story together.

02:26.735 --> 02:31.333
Record retained recurring value,
expansion value, and one-time value

02:31.333 --> 02:31.919
separately.

02:32.169 --> 02:36.217
Those are proposed reporting
categories, not a claim that HubSpot

02:36.217 --> 02:37.673
creates them automatically.

02:38.333 --> 02:42.352
Separate linked opportunities may help
when renewal and expansion have

02:42.352 --> 02:44.029
different owners or outcomes.

02:44.279 --> 02:46.669
Keep their purchase relationship
traceable.

02:46.919 --> 02:50.503
Never sum a combined parent amount
and the same child amounts.

02:50.753 --> 02:54.500
A shared purchase identity does not
prove that quoting across those

02:54.500 --> 02:56.299
deals works automatically.

02:56.967 --> 03:00.487
HubSpot's deal ARR uses recurring line
items.

03:00.737 --> 03:04.959
Its separate Enterprise Revenue
Analytics uses manually maintained

03:04.959 --> 03:08.267
recurring revenue fields, including a
monthly amount.

03:08.517 --> 03:12.293
A custom report is another route, with
account-dependent access.

03:12.543 --> 03:16.703
Choose one route deliberately and
verify the units, dates, and filters.

03:17.367 --> 03:22.337
Define what one report row represents:
for example, one purchase component.

03:22.587 --> 03:26.598
Adding associated contacts or
activities can multiply rows.

03:26.848 --> 03:30.149
Add a deliberate duplicate to the test
data and check that

03:30.149 --> 03:32.224
the money total stays unchanged.

03:32.474 --> 03:35.972
A distinct deal count alone does not
guarantee that a money

03:35.972 --> 03:36.997
sum is correct.

03:37.667 --> 03:39.288
Now test a different outcome.

03:39.538 --> 03:42.461
The renewal succeeds, but the
expansion is lost.

03:42.711 --> 03:45.697
Closing ARR should stay at twelve
thousand dollars.

03:45.947 --> 03:49.720
Preserve the proposed
three-thousand-dollar expansion and

03:49.720 --> 03:53.845
its lost outcome in history, rather than
deleting the only evidence

03:53.845 --> 03:55.035
that it was ever offered.

03:55.700 --> 03:59.698
If the retained baseline falls to ten
thousand and expansion adds

03:59.698 --> 04:03.700
three thousand, closing ARR becomes
thirteen thousand.

04:03.950 --> 04:08.298
Also test future start dates: a signed
expansion is not active

04:08.298 --> 04:09.582
before its effective date.

04:09.832 --> 04:14.080
Record expected and observed results
separately; these examples are

04:14.080 --> 04:17.427
reporting tests, not executed HubSpot
outcomes.

04:18.100 --> 04:21.976
Give the commission process the
classified amounts, owners and policy

04:21.976 --> 04:22.452
version.

04:22.702 --> 04:26.178
Do not assume every dollar earns the
same rate, or that

04:26.178 --> 04:28.825
ARR growth is always the commission
base.

04:29.075 --> 04:33.822
Renewal credit, expansion credit and
one-time services must follow the

04:33.822 --> 04:36.115
company's actual compensation policy.

04:36.767 --> 04:40.489
The companion pack contains a
classification dictionary, a

04:40.489 --> 04:43.529
reconciliation sheet and reporting test
cases.

04:43.779 --> 04:47.927
Agree the definitions first, trace each
value to its source, and

04:47.927 --> 04:50.798
compare the expected result with the
actual report.

04:51.048 --> 04:54.504
Fix discrepancies before using the
report for decisions.

04:55.167 --> 04:58.985
One purchase can include renewal,
expansion and one-time work.

04:59.235 --> 05:03.312
In this example, the purchase is
sixteen thousand five hundred dollars,

05:03.312 --> 05:08.195
closing ARR is fifteen thousand, and
recurring growth is three thousand.

05:08.445 --> 05:12.136
Keep those meanings distinct, and
count each contribution once.
